Cell["\<\
Use this function when a term in the model preserves only part of the \
original symmetry. The selected operations generate the symmetry subgroup \
that is to remain, while all atoms are kept.\
\>", "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"d203ad6a-1dcb-452e-a58e-33a479eceed7"],

Cell["\<\
If the subgroup no longer relates all atoms of a Wyckoff orbit, that orbit is \
split into separate entries of the new wyckoffposition input.\
\>", "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"70578d97-10e9-41b2-875e-63be2ca35924"],

Cell["\<\
The function only writes a new set of init rules; it does not change the \
model by itself. Check the new Wyckoff positions and symmetry operations, \
then evaluate init@@rules. Use {} when only the identity is to remain.\
\>", "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"fe85ee7c-bf3c-4de0-9f69-7ce695805a35"]
}, Closed]],

